en:
let me be drunk on devotion — and angry with the world,
and pitying it — then laugh, and rise up, and shout:
śiva! — enough.

i am dull, i am weighed with sorrow, i am afraid of old age's flaws,
i am without power — i have taken refuge in you, o śambhu;
so calculate what's left.

may all my time — even the endless kind — pass
in the happiness of union with your worship;
that alone is what i crave.

let the yoked one meditate thus — the human attains swiftly:
she whom i have declared before,
the supreme aghorī power.
